{
  "_schema": "Tax form structure: jurisdiction-year -> form -> cells (and optional blocks for zero-to-many sections).",
  "_comments": [
    "Cell keys can be line numbers (\"1\", \"2\") or names (\"3a\", \"standard_deduction\").",
    "manual_entry: true = user fills; false = computed from equation. All amounts in USD.",
    "required_rule: requiredness rule for the cell. Use \"always\", \"optional\", or a formula string evaluated like an equation to determine when the cell is required.",
    "description: matches what is written on the form or worksheet. explanation: more detail when needed (can be same as description).",
    "blocks: repeating sections (0 to many entries). Each block has item_cells (schema for one entry), entries (array of objects), and optional min_entries/max_entries.",
    "Block cell naming: block_id.index.field_name -- e.g. w2.0.box_1, dependents.1.ssn. In equations: sum(w2.*.box_1) = sum over all W-2 entries. Line 1 flows from w2 block.",
    "W-2: employer-furnished; sample form https://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-prior/fw2--2025.pdf",
    "User-entered sources: Data from employer/payer-furnished forms (W-2, 1099s, 1098s) is entered by the user from the forms they received; we need these forms in the system and they have no in-app instructions.",
    "Multi-entry cells: Some form boxes allow multiple entries (e.g. W-2 Box 12: code + amount per line). Use type \"repeating\" with item_cells and entries. Reference: block_id.index.field_name.sub_index.sub_field -- e.g. w2.0.box_12.0.code, w2.0.box_12.1.amount."
  ],
